+The three workflows in `n8n/` ("Lead Desk: Web Form Intake", "Lead Desk: Email Intake", "Lead Desk: Duplicate Test (10 at once)"; files `desk-form.json`, `desk-webhook.json`, `proof.json`) were built in the n8n version of `versions.md` through n8n's REST interface and run against the desk and the demo servers. Section 1 of this page describes them (see "Licence" for what you may do with them). Findings, in plain words (all from the author's own run on 2026-11-09; no log is shipped; counts and timings can differ from run to run):
 
-* **In that run n8n answered 200 whenever the desk answered**, even when the desk said 201 (new) or 202 (review). The verdict (`new`, `duplicate`, `review`) is only in the reply body, so a caller must read the body, not the status number.
 * **A desk refusal shows as an n8n error.** If the desk answers 400 (bad request) or 413 (too large), the caller gets HTTP 500 from n8n (`Error in workflow`). Because the sending box has Retry On Fail on (3 tries, 1 second apart; see `n8n/desk-form.json`), n8n sends such a refused request 3 times in all, so the desk counts each refused call 3 times.
-* **Restart tolerance is short.** With the desk restarted at once, the second try succeeded (the answer came after about one second, as the author timed it). With the desk down for a few seconds, all three tries were used up and the call failed with 500 (within about 2 seconds). For longer outages raise the number of tries or the wait.
